    {
      "source": "hackernews",
      "subsource": "news.ycombinator.com",
      "category": "ai",
      "title": "Born Against, or why hobby programming communities are against LLM usage",
      "url": "https://blog.fogus.me/llm/born-against.html",
      "discuss_url": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49187061",
      "score": 321,
      "comments": 359,
      "author": "lladnar",
      "published": "2026-08-05T18:37:49Z",
      "bullets": [
        "Automated PR generation increases triage overhead for open-source maintainers, flooding repositories with unverified, difficult-to-audit LLM code.",
        "Hobby programmers reject tools like GitHub Copilot because offloading synthesis undermines skill acquisition, deep learning, and personal mastery.",
        "LLM code generation introduces subtle security risks, including hallucinated package dependencies, licensing conflicts, and unvetted logic errors."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/programming",
      "category": "engineering",
      "title": "The following is a valid DOS COM executable",
      "url": "https://oldbytes.space/@gloriouscow/117045701876951834",
      "discuss_url": "https://lobste.rs/s/o8ttys",
      "score": 9,
      "comments": 1,
      "author": "dsr",
      "published": "2026-08-06T11:37:30Z",
      "bullets": [
        "MS-DOS .COM binaries lack structured headers like PE or ELF, executing raw bytes directly at memory offset 0x0100 in 16-bit mode.",
        "ASCII-executable polyglots exploit overlapping x86 opcode mappings with printable character sets to construct dual-purpose text and binary files.",
        "Format ambiguity risks allow attackers to bypass file-type validation, demonstrating parser differential vulnerabilities in security scanners and legacy interpreters."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "lobsters",
      "subsource": "lobste.rs/security",
      "category": "security",
      "title": "tl;dv (Too Lazy; Didn't Validate): 181,874 Meetings Left Wide Open",
